// Isolde's Last Camp (LastCamp_1; bible 7.3 step 1). Just across the line. Her tent, her lamp still lit, her complete
// atlas. Reveal 5.2: she stole the sixth keystone from the Guild's Vault to return it to Corvin, and walked in to
// find Ilse and tell her Wren was alive. She had no tether. She believed Wren would follow and could cross.
// The pages speak in her plain voice. Reading them starts Act 3.

title: LastCamp_Isolde
---
<<if has_flag("act3.started")>>
    Pages: Every place I walked, drawn. Don't anchor what I've drawn. You know why now. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pages: Journeyman. You crossed. I knew you could. I didn't know if you would.
Pages: The Vault's sixth slot. I took it. Voss let me, or didn't look. I never decided which.
Pages: It's Corvin's stone. I'm taking it back to him. And I'm finding Ilse.
Pages: Ilse should know you're alive. She'll tell you why that matters. I won't. It's hers.
Pages: No tether. I didn't want one. I thought you'd follow. Here you are.
Pages: The Guild will say I'm dead. They'll say it quickly. Ask yourself why so quickly.
Pages: This is the whole atlas. Every place I walked. Take it. East is the Lantern.
-> She stole it. For him.
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
-> I'm coming, Isolde.
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> ...
    <<voice drift blank>>
<<flag isolde.atlas_taken 1>>
<<flag act3.started 1>>
===
